// `foreach` IS a window: it holds a borrowing iterator over its operand for the whole body, so the
// operand is FROZEN there — growing it mid-loop is a compile error, not a runtime panic.
//
// This fixture was a `tests/trap/` case until the freeze reached `foreach`. It is finding 7's exact
// repro: `reserve()` reallocs without going through `add`/`put`, so the mods counter stayed untouched and
// the loop read the freed buffer (ASan-proven, zero `unsafe` tokens). The counter is now bumped in
// `growTo` where the relocation happens, but that is depth — this rule is what makes the mistake
// unnameable rather than merely trapped.
// The `Map` arm — `reserve` rehashes into fresh key/value/state buffers and frees the old ones.
import std::collections::{Map};

fn int main() {
    Map<int32, int32> m = Map.withCapacity(capacity: 8);
    m.put(key: 1, value: 10); m.put(key: 2, value: 20);
    int32 t = 0;
    foreach (int32 v in m.values()) { m.reserve(n: 4096); t = t + v; }
    return t;
}
